It's definitely an abuse in my mind.  Even worse than polypiling.  But I 
love it.

A few pretty minor things I learned:

Engrave with your dagger until it's too dull.  It will be -3 and soon 
thoroughly corroded too.  

Get yourself a stethoscope.  Puddings with N hp will split into two 
puddings with (N-1)/2 each.  All puddings with 3 or more hp will split and 
not die (with a suitable weapon).

Learn healing or extra healing and cast it on the puddings if they're too 
weak.  Like fertilizing your farm.

If there's no sink and altar on the same level, consider dragging a corpse 
from somewhere else and then cast undead turning on it.

It's nice to have an ice box near your altar.  If you have a wand of undead 
turning you don't have to worry so much about killing your last pudding.  

Zap the first one with slow monster before you split it.  They'll ALL be 
slow.

Manage your luck to avoid crowning.  You'll get lots more stuff from your 
Deity.

I keep a pudding trapped in a door with boulders like this:

  --------
  |.......
  |.......
``P`..._(.
  |..@....
  --------

That way I can go away and come back, or read spellbooks or strip naked or 
whatever, and I don't have to worry about being disturbed.  At the same 
time I can start a new generation whenever I want.

Sometimes when I kill one, another pudding steps on the corpse.  When I 
kill them a bunch at a time with a spell, it makes it really inconvenient 
to collect the corpses.  With a ring of conflict the puddings will attack 
each other (they seem not to do ANY damage) and they will HOLD STILL while 
I collect the corpses.  I've considered burning the E-word on a whole 
area..  then they'd never step on the corpses and I wouldn't have to watch 
all the "The black pudding misses the black pudding" messages.

